# A frame addressed to a call number we do not have, hand-built from RFC 5456
# §6.9.2: "An INVAL is sent as a response to a received message that is not
# valid. This occurs when an IAX peer sends a message on a call after the
# remote peer has hung up its end."
#
# Our source call number is 1; this frame is addressed to destination call
# number 9, which is nobody. The expected answer is an INVAL (§8.4 subclass
# 0x0a) mirroring the pair — source 9, destination 0x0042 — and echoing the
# time-stamp so the peer can match it to the frame that provoked it.

# PING, source 0x0042, destination 0x0009, ts 100, OSeq 0, ISeq 1, IAX/PING.
8042 0009 00000064 00 01 06 02
